<title>CHILE: M.Blancos reports higher copper output.</title>
<headline>M.Blancos reports higher copper output.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Copper production in the first quarter at Minorco SA's Mantos Blancos mine in Chile was 31,764 tonnes, up 17 percent over the same period last year, Empresa Minera de Mantos Blancos said.</p>
<p>The figure, including output from both the Mantos Blancos and Mantoverde divisions, was comprised 66 percent of cathodes and 34 percent of copper contained in concentrates.</p>
<p>The mine is located in northern Chile's second region near the city of Antofagasta.</p>
<p>((--Roger Atwood, Santiago newsroom +56-2-699-5595 x211))</p>
